  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Solo devotional supplications in classical Arabic sung by Egyptian munshids trained in Qur'an recitation, usually unaccompanied and improvised through the maqamat, and broadcast before the dawn prayer and during Ramadan on Egyptian Radio, above all in the 1960s and 1970s. Sayed Naqshabandi and Nasr el-Din Tobar are its most celebrated radio voices.",
